---
import LabsLayout from "../../layouts/labs.astro";
---

<LabsLayout title="Scenario B — PostgreSQL staged load — Querial Labs" active="b">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">Scenario B</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">PostgreSQL staged load</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                Minimal Parquet path. Extract products from SQL Server to an artifact,
                then Staged Database SQL upserts into PostgreSQL. This is the smallest
                lab that needs Artifacts + DuckDB.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/labs/adventureworks/downloads/scenario-b-postgres.zip" download
               class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-querial-indigo px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:opacity-90">
                Download scenario-b-postgres.zip
            </a>
            <a href="/labs/run-through" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Load and test
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/devops-artifacts" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Artifacts docs
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>Package</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Package <code class="text-foreground">aw-scenario-b</code>, pipeline <code class="text-foreground">aw_scenario_b</code>.</li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">aw-source</code> sqlserver — extract.</li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">aw-pg-dest</code> postgresql — migrations + staged load.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Topology</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>extract_product  (ROOT, database-query-to-parquet → aw-source)
  └─(artifact_available)→ load_product  (staged-database-sql → aw-pg-dest)</code></pre>
            <p>
                The sink must not start until artifact <code class="text-foreground">product</code>
                exists. That is <code class="text-foreground">artifact_available</code>, not a
                generic “succeeded” edge (though the extract must succeed to produce the file).
            </p>

            <h2>Migrations (aw-pg-dest)</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">001_create_schema</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">004_create_product</code> — <code class="text-foreground">aw.product</code></li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Steps and config</h2>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">extract_product</code> —
                <code class="text-foreground">database-query-to-parquet</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">config.outputName = product</code> (no file extension).
                SQL reads AdventureWorks product columns.
            </p>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">load_product</code> —
                <code class="text-foreground">staged-database-sql</code>.
                One list row with
                <code class="text-foreground">from_step: extract_product</code>, column
                contracts (id, name, product_number, color, costs, dates),
                <code class="text-foreground">transaction.mode: stage-and-execute</code>.
                SQL upserts from the bare token <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ stage }}"}</code>
                because this sink has one inbound file. There is no ArtifactToTable
                auto-copy.
                <a href="/docs/developer-handler-contracts" class="text-link hover:underline">Handler contracts</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Flags</h2>
            <p>
                Required: <code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:Artifacts</code>
                and <code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:DuckDb</code> (environment
                often <code class="text-foreground">Querial__Extensions__Artifacts=true</code>
                and <code class="text-foreground">Querial__Extensions__DuckDb=true</code>).
            </p>

            <h2>Walkthrough extras</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li>Create Development endpoints: source = AdventureWorks SQL Server; dest = PostgreSQL warehouse.</li>
                <li>Run Graph: extract shows an artifact in the inspector; load stays not-ready until the file exists, then stages and executes.</li>
                <li>If extract succeeds and load fails, retry / failed-cone is an operator action on run details — not on the canvas. See <a href="/docs/devops-retry" class="text-link hover:underline">Retry and failed-cone recovery</a>. In-run auto-retry of the staged load is off by default (writes are unsafe) — <a href="/docs/developer-retry" class="text-link hover:underline">Step retry policies</a>.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Verify</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM aw.product;</code></pre>
            <p>Compare to <code class="text-foreground">Production.Product</code> on the source (the extract SQL’s filter).</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</LabsLayout>
